d":"c87c8f8a-0e1a-46c2-a2e8-6a61905f49da","position":{"commit_sha":"31755737d9729a98b035432f33d8b08c3292fc4e","position":"1788310624061076704-c87c8f8a-0e1a-46c2-a2e8-6a61905f49da"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fc3acd12681c98a68c3f981f63bc3b8e5a264584ff9a4c68c46524b2af25ebd7","event_uuid":"ed8db782-257a-4c6b-8126-921b2a776202","position":{"commit_sha":"0ef6541d61a216e283ba435017024f8a24e3c894","position":"1788310820601733382-ed8db782-257a-4c6b-8126-921b2a776202"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"77598e5431d9f8102200b515b59de76770660323239aec3958ad28a44420c153","event_uuid":"a28f94d4-53c5-4a87-9e8e-394c83404f0f","position":{"commit_sha":"559974d9313f41380ca5f7fcd083ca02381812b1","position":"1788311408386011478-a28f94d4-53c5-4a87-9e8e-394c83404f0f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fd4953b3ee989fde4225d9360c4b0792ceeebb0e8911451a55c0f33d2625e194","event_uuid":"088db37f-35a5-47b3-822e-1f67c029420a","position":{"commit_sha":"f85b0b2dba6281a2aa86fcfac055132e11907dbb","position":"1788311869397481001-088db37f-35a5-47b3-822e-1f67c029420a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Decision recorded: approach A + B APPROVED (operator authorization, 2026-09-01)\n\nThe operator approved BOTH parts of the durable fix as the direction. Implementation specifics (exact thresholds, code seams) proceed through the normal plan-review gate.\n\n**A — acute-pressure emergency reclaim tier.** Keep the 5 GB warm build-cache at normal disk levels, but above a hard threshold (~90% used, above the existing 80% soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`) escalate `prune_docker_caches()` to `docker builder prune -f` with keep→0, and record bytes actually freed (not invocation count). Completes the documented intent of 28f9-535c (pressure-triggered prune), e2c5-f09b (5 GB cap), and applies 9bc0-1200's lesson (\"measure effect, not calls\"). OSS precedent: kubelet soft-vs-hard eviction thresholds; BuildKit GC keepBytes normally / aggressive prune under pressure.\n\n**B — near-full admission control in the review clone path.** Before materializing a snapshot (`src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py` / `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`), if free disk is below a hard floor, DEFER the review via ADR 0069's existing retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral path (vote-less, budgeted) instead of cloning into ENOSPC. This prevents a self-inflicted disk-full from being misclassified as a `coverage-gap (review-error)` and burning the retry budget to a spurious fail-closed −1 (exactly what happened to change 2481 in this incident). OSS precedent: Jenkins disk-space node monitor (marks agent offline below threshold), Kubernetes ephemeral-storage eviction, Zuul executor disk governor.\n\n**Both, not one:** A frees space but a burst refills; B holds the line but leaves the disk pinned; together they self-heal. **EBS growth explicitly rejected** as the fix (workload-bound growth + %-based trigger → only delays the identical wall); acceptable only as a throwaway unwedge lever.\n\nDispatching an implementation agent to plan-review → claim → implement (held-out TDD) → land through Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) → close.","timestamp":1788308413931818007}],"created_at":1788304689530604559,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9efe5ac6-42ce-4c3e-9d11-dd2bd3926158","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"28f9-535c-ce9c-4583"},{"link_uuid":"2b387593-6ef6-4a0d-805a-86d7d2b1cfd4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9bc0-1200-1451-44bb"},{"link_uuid":"457c31a3-417b-4310-9773-58e72c460868","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nOn 2026-09-01 the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on `rebar-gerrit` fail-closed reviews because root disk reached 91-95%; review clones/materializations hit ENOSPC and surfaced as `coverage-gap (review-error)`. Change 2481 exhausted its retry budget to a spurious LLM-Review -1. Recovery required manual `docker builder prune -f` without `--keep-storage`, proving automated prune could not reclaim below its 5GB build-cache floor. Operator approved implementing fixes A+B.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` always runs `docker builder prune -f --keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`, even on acute pressure/no-op tick paths. At 5.244GB cache, automated prune freed ~0.\n2. The review hot path starts clones/materializations without checking free disk first. `voter.py` clones into `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` on the root temp volume; `repo_snapshot.py` materializes into the snapshot-store volume.\n\n## Approved implementation plan\n\n### A. Acute pressure reclaim tier\n\nKeep normal warm-cache behavior unchanged. Add `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` default 90, above soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT=80`. When root used-% is at/above hard threshold, `prune_docker_caches()` escalates BuildKit reclaim to `docker builder prune -f` with keep->0 (no `--keep-storage`), best-effort/non-fatal and `timeout 120` bounded like existing docker calls. Measure before/after root filesystem bytes and log bytes actually freed; success evidence is `bytes_freed > 0`, not invocation.\n\n### B. Low-disk admission control\n\nAdd target-path free-space helper in `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py` (`shutil.disk_usage(path)`) and `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` default 2. This is a hard pre-clone admission floor; existing janitor watermarks remain cleanup targets.\n\nCheck target volume before cloning/materializing:\n\n- In `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`, before `TemporaryDirectory` / `gc.clone_change_ref`, measure `tempfile.gettempdir()`.\n- In `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` / `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`, measure the snapshot-store path before attested snapshot clone/materialize.\n\nRepresent low disk explicitly. Snapshot admission raises a dedicated `LowDiskError` (or returns an equivalent low-disk sentinel) with target path/free/floor. `gate_source.py` maps that condition into structured coverage as `coverage[\"low_disk\"] = True` and preserves details; `adapter._coverage_gap_reason` gains a first branch `if coverage.get(\"low_disk\"): return \"low-disk\"`. Do not let low disk fall through to generic `review-error`.\n\nFor the Gerrit voter pre-clone guard, synthesize a decision with `verdict=\"BLOCK\"`, `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, and first line `[LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)] ...`. Define `_TAG_SUFFIXES[\"low-disk\"] = \"BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)\"`; add `low-disk` to `adapter.RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS`; keep `retrigger.py` parsing the existing `coverage-gap (<reason>)` grammar.\n\nIn `_handle_retryable_gap`, add explicit low-disk semantics. Under budget it defers vote-less like existing ADR 0069 retryable gaps. At/over the low-disk budget it returns `deferred_result` with a terminal status such as `deferred-exhausted`, `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, writes/logs an operator-visible neutral Gerrit comment/status explaining low disk exhausted retry holdback and that a `recheck`/new patchset will retry after disk remediation, but leaves labels unchanged: no `LLM-Review -1`, no `append_retries_exhausted_note`, no `VOTER_ERROR`. This converges safely by making the change non-submittable due to missing LLM vote while avoiding a false code veto; explicit recheck/new patchset remains the recovery path after the host is healthy. Existing exhaustion behavior for non-low-disk review errors/coverage gaps is unchanged. Document in ADR 0069, ADR 0077, `docs/review-policy.md`, and `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Hard-pressure reclaim: root used-% >= `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` with enough reclaimable build-cache excess causes emergency keep->0 builder prune, logs/measures `bytes_freed > 0`, and fixture returns below soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` and/or `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`.\n- [ ] Warm-cache regression: below `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT`, `prune_docker_caches()` still uses `--keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`.\n- [ ] Review-bot low-disk admission: below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` on `tempfile.gettempdir()`, `voter.py` does not create the clone and defers retryably/vote-less through ADR 0069; proof by focused voter test asserting no clone/vote.\n- [ ] Exhausted low-disk budget: labels remain unchanged/no `LLM-Review -1`, with a neutral operator-visible exhausted-deferral result recoverable by recheck/new patchset; proof contrasts `low-disk` with `review-error` exhaustion.\n- [ ] Snapshot low-disk admission: below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` on the snapshot-store volume, materialization aborts before clone with `coverage[\"low_disk\"]` -> `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`; proof around `repo_snapshot.py` / `gate_source.py` / adapter coverage routing.\n- [ ] Distinct semantics: literal suffix `BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)` and routing tests distinguish low-disk from genuine coverage/review errors.\n- [ ] Portability: all reclaim/admission logic is in-process/operation-linked, with no CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest <focused low-disk review admission/voter tests> -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## File impact\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`; `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`; `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`; `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`; `docs/review-policy.md`; `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`; `docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md`; `docs/adr/0077-code-review-voter-four-pass-rewire.md`; focused tests.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"add DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT hard pressure tier, measured root bytes freed, and keep-storage=0 emergency build-cache prune"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py","reason":"helper-level RED/GREEN coverage for normal warm-cache prune vs hard-pressure emergency prune and measured bytes freed"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py","reason":"script/no-op-tick disk-pressure behavior proving hard-tier reclaim attempts return below soft threshold in the induced fixture"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","reason":"export/reuse target-path volume free-space computation for admission control"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"guard snapshot-store materialization before clone using the target store volume floor"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","reason":"surface low-disk materialization deferral through gate acquisition path where applicable"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","reason":"pre-clone admission check, synthesized low-disk decision, and explicit _handle_retryable_gap low-disk exhausted-budget no-vote arm"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"add low-disk to retryable gap reason vocabulary with _TAG_SUFFIXES['low-disk']='BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)'"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py","reason":"confirm/adjust classifier handles coverage-gap (low-disk) tag grammar without changing unrelated stems"},{"path":"docs/review-policy.md","reason":"document the new low-disk vote-message tag/tunable and no-vote exhausted-budget disposition"},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md","reason":"update shipped reviewer/author guide coverage-gap subreason vocabulary and low-disk terminal no-vote semantics"},{"path":"docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md","reason":"document low-disk as a special retryable admission-deferral reason with no-vote exhausted-budget disposition"},{"path":"docs/adr/0077-code-review-voter-four-pass-rewire.md","reason":"update voter retryable-gap exhaustion invariant for low-disk special case"},{"path":"tests","reason":"focused held-out unit/integration coverage for low-disk vote-less deferral, exhausted-budget no-vote behavior, genuine coverage gap contrast, config effect, and warm-cache regression"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["disk-pressure","review-bot","defect-escape","infra"],"ticket_id":"3cef-c948-68ba-40fd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Disk-pressure reclaim cannot reach the build-cache floor under acute pressure, and the review clone path has no near-full admission control — review-bot fail-closes again","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["eb63